INTERVIA - Abstract
Problem Statement
Traditional technical interview preparation often relies on static question banks and lacks personalized assessment, real-time interaction, and meaningful performance feedback. Candidates may practice common interview questions but do not receive an interview experience that adapts to their technical skills, resume background, answer quality, and time constraints. There is therefore a need for an intelligent system that can simulate a technical interview and provide automated evaluation and personalized feedback.
Technical Solution
The proposed system, INTERVIA, is an AI-powered web-based mock interview platform developed using React for the frontend and FastAPI for the backend. The system uses REST APIs for communication between the frontend and backend and uses a database for storing candidate, interview-session, and evaluation information. AI-based evaluation is used to analyze candidate responses and assign scores and feedback. The system also incorporates resume processing to extract relevant candidate information from uploaded PDF/DOCX resumes.
Solution Proposed / Implemented
INTERVIA provides candidate authentication, technical skill selection, resume uploading, resume intelligence, adaptive technical questioning, programming/problem-solving questions, aptitude questions, timed interviews, voice-based interaction, camera support, AI-based answer evaluation, and performance analysis. Each interview consists of up to 20 questions with a 20-minute overall time limit and a 60-second limit per question. The system stores interview results and presents the candidate's performance through a dedicated dashboard. By combining AI evaluation, adaptive questioning, resume-based personalization, and interactive interview features, INTERVIA provides a more realistic and personalized environment for technical interview preparation.

